---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/Icon.astro';
import Architecture from '../../../components/Architecture.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Crypto exchange development"
  description="Explore Soft Task crypto exchange development for centralised and decentralised platforms: interfaces, execution, wallets, settlement, reconciliation and operations."
  dark
>
  <section class="exchange-cover">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/services/blockchain-engineering/">Blockchain & Web3</a>
        <span>/ Exchange development</span>
      </div>
      <h1>
        More than an
        <br />
        order on a screen.
      </h1>
      <div>
        <p>
          An exchange connects an experience to an execution model, an asset-control model and an
          operating record. Soft Task develops the technology around those relationships.
        </p>
        <a class="button light" href="/contact/?service=blockchain-engineering">
          Discuss exchange development <Icon />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="exchange-models wrap">
    <h2>
      Start with the
      <br />
      exchange model.
    </h2>
    <div>
      <article>
        <span>Centralised exchange</span>
        <h3>Coordinate the platform’s systems.</h3>
        <p>
          Define the relationship between accounts, balances, order handling, matching, wallets and
          settlement. Integration with onboarding, reporting and operational controls belongs in the
          platform architecture.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Trading interfaces and account workflows</li>
          <li>Order handling and matching-engine integration</li>
          <li>Wallet, deposit and withdrawal workflows</li>
          <li>Balance records and reconciliation</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>Decentralised exchange</span>
        <h3>Connect the application to the protocol.</h3>
        <p>
          Define how the interface connects to contracts and liquidity mechanisms. Explain signing,
          network fees, transaction confirmation and failure states so users can understand the
          action they are taking.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Wallet-connected application interfaces</li>
          <li>Swap and liquidity workflow integrations</li>
          <li>Smart-contract development and testing</li>
          <li>On-chain event and transaction indexing</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="exchange-architecture wrap">
    <Architecture kind="web3" />
    <div>
      <h2>
        Keep the records
        <br />
        in agreement.
      </h2>
      <p>
        Order state, balances, transfers and on-chain confirmations may update at different times.
        Define which record is authoritative and how the system handles duplicates, delays and
        failed dependencies.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reconciliation and exception handling deserve their own acceptance criteria. A normal
        successful trade does not demonstrate how the platform behaves during an outage or a partial
        failure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="exchange-readiness">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Before a launch decision.</h2>
      <div class="readiness-list">
        <article>
          <h3>Validate the flows</h3>
          <p>
            Test account access, order lifecycle, deposits, withdrawals and failure scenarios with
            representative conditions.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Assign asset control</h3>
          <p>
            Document custody, signing permissions, operational access and recovery responsibilities.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Prepare operations</h3>
          <p>Agree monitoring, reconciliation, incident escalation and release ownership.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Confirm external requirements</h3>
          <p>
            Licensing, independent reviews, banking and liquidity arrangements require their own
            owners and approvals.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="product-next wrap">
    <div>
      <h2>
        Define the platform
        <br />
        before the build.
      </h2>
      <p>
        Bring the intended markets, exchange model, custody approach and integration requirements.
        We can then shape the engineering scope around them.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="button" href="/contact/?service=blockchain-engineering">
      Start the conversation <Icon />
    </a>
  </section>
</Layout>
